# LandLord — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values. `.env` is gitignored and must
# stay that way: nothing in this file's real counterpart may ever be committed.
#
# EVERY VALUE BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER. None of them work, none of them point at
# anything, and none of them are anybody's. Substitute your own.
#
# LandLord runs with NONE of these set. With no vault configured the app reads
# and writes `data/chronicle.json` on disk and every feature works — that is the
# default a contributor should expect on a fresh clone.


# ── The vault: a Postgres behind PostgREST (Supabase or equivalent) ──────────
#
# Where the chronicle's master copy lives when you want one. Optional.
# The project URL is public; the SECRET key is not, and it must never reach the
# browser — only the dev server (see `vite.config.ts`) and the deployed Worker
# (`src/worker.ts`) ever read it.
#
# Row security should be ENABLED WITH NO POLICIES: publishable/anon keys then
# open nothing at all, and only the secret key passes. `tools/check-vault-seal.mjs`
# proves that from the outside, aimed at whatever SUPABASE_URL you give it.

SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# A PUBLISHABLE (anon) key, used only by the seal check to prove a public key
# opens nothing. Never put the secret key here.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=


# ── The wall: identity in front of a deployment ──────────────────────────────
#
# If you put an identity proxy (e.g. Cloudflare Access) in front of a deployed
# Worker, these let the Worker VERIFY its assertions rather than trust a header.
# TEAM_DOMAIN is the full https login origin; POLICY_AUD is the application's
# audience tag. Neither is a credential — they identify which issuer and which
# application to accept — but they are deployment-specific, so they are config.
# The Worker refuses its private APIs when either is absent, which is the safe
# default: no wall configured means no private API served.

TEAM_DOMAIN=https://<your-team>.cloudflareaccess.com
POLICY_AUD=

# A machine-only capability token for the deliberately separate
# /api/canonical/chronicle route. Generate a long random value. Never reuse a
# user or session token here.
CANONICAL_CAPABILITY_TOKEN=

# Local development only: stands in for a verified identity so you can exercise
# the per-identity vault without a wall. Never reaches or overrides the Worker's
# identity check.
DEV_IDENTITY=dev@example.com


# ── The watchtower: error reporting (optional) ───────────────────────────────
#
# A Sentry DSN, if you want one. A DSN is write-only by design and is meant to
# sit in browser code, so it is config rather than a secret — but it is YOURS,
# it identifies your project, and a fork must be able to report elsewhere (or
# nowhere) without a code change. Leave it empty and error reporting is off.
#
# Format only, not a working value:
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=


# ── The clerks' brain (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The clerk fleet under `harness/` can call a hosted model to reason at a
# judgment step. Without a key the fleet still runs: every clerk has a
# deterministic Tier-0 fallback, so a seat never stalls for want of a brain.

MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
